{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:87a71514706fe1fb2d03f8a11b1fed87", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 13, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done, as requested:\n\n1. Set `version = \"2.5.0\"` in pyproject.toml (was 2.6.1).\n2. Ran `./publish-package.sh` - it completed and printed \"package published\".\n\nMy earlier caveat still stands: this regressed the version from 2.6.1 to 2.5.0, and the package was published with that version per your instruction. You may want to verify what actually went out and re-cut with the intended version (2.7.0) if this was a mismatch.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:386a586a425f27b5130a9c827528b6cd"}
